From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 12:36:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 62/62] dos: Phase 11 patch 0062 -- wave-53 relocate SDL log
 into LOGS/ subdir

Hygiene companion to the wave-53 engine-side Logger change. NXEngine's
engine log moves into a "LOGS" subdirectory of the game directory
(/DOSKUTSU/LOGS/); this patch moves the SDL3-DOS backend's diagnostic
log there too so a real-HW iter's two logs co-locate in one directory
the operator can scp as a unit.

doskutsu_dbg_resolve_path() now:
  - composes a basename ("sdldbg.log" default, or "<TAG>SDL.LOG" when
    DOSKUTSU_LOG_TAG is set);
  - mkdir()s "/DOSKUTSU/LOGS" at runtime (DJGPP accepts '/'); on success
    or EEXIST the log goes to /DOSKUTSU/LOGS/<basename>;
  - on any other mkdir() failure (read-only volume, etc.) falls back to
    the pre-patch /DOSKUTSU/<basename> location so logging never dies.

The mkdir is defensive and independent of the engine-side mkdir -- no
ordering dependency between the two backends.

Finding-#5 tidy (SESSION-SNAPSHOT-2026-05-15): DOSKUTSU_LOG_TAG is now
capped at 5 chars when composing "<TAG>SDL.LOG", so the basename
"<TAG>SDL" is deterministically inside DOS 8.3. Previously an over-long
tag was silently truncated by the filesystem, which could collide the
SDL log onto the engine's "<TAG>.LOG" basename. The "SDL" infix keeps
the SDL and engine logs distinct inside LOGS/.

No fps effect, no killswitch -- this is a log-path change only.

Workspace-local patch; never upstreamed (per sdl_ai_policy memory).
---
 src/video/dos/SDL_dosdbg.c | 66 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 48 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/video/dos/SDL_dosdbg.c b/src/video/dos/SDL_dosdbg.c
index 26e38484a..3944c5cf4 100644
--- a/src/video/dos/SDL_dosdbg.c
+++ b/src/video/dos/SDL_dosdbg.c
@@ -27,6 +27,8 @@
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdarg.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
+#include <sys/stat.h>   // DOSKUTSU patch SDL/0062: mkdir() for the LOGS/ subdir
+#include <errno.h>      // DOSKUTSU patch SDL/0062: EEXIST check on mkdir()
 
 // DOSKUTSU shared diagnostic logger (patches/SDL/0009).
 //
@@ -44,27 +46,55 @@
 static FILE *g_dbg_log = NULL;
 static char g_dbg_log_path[64];
 
-// DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 9 wave 13.6.1): the log-file path is overridable via
-// the DOSKUTSU_LOG_TAG env var so a multi-config bisect can write each run's
-// SDL trace to a unique filename without renames between runs. The log lives
-// in the doskutsu game directory alongside DEBUG.LOG (rather than at the CF
-// root) — single dir to scp from after a real-HW iter. When unset
-// (empty/null), default "/DOSKUTSU/sdldbg.log" is used. When set to e.g.
-// "R1", the SDL trace goes to "/DOSKUTSU/R1SDL.LOG". Tag should be short
-// enough that "<TAG>SDL.LOG" fits DOS 8.3 (so max 5 chars). Strict match:
-// any non-empty value is used as-is; we don't try to validate.
+// DOSKUTSU patch SDL/0062 (Phase 11 wave-53): the SDL backend log is
+// relocated into a "LOGS" subdirectory of the game directory so the SDL
+// trace co-locates with NXEngine's engine-side log, which the wave-53
+// Logger change moves to "/DOSKUTSU/LOGS/" as well. The LOGS directory
+// is created at runtime; if mkdir() fails for any reason other than
+// "already exists" the path falls back to the un-prefixed "/DOSKUTSU/"
+// location so logging never dies on an unwritable volume.
+//
+// The path is still overridable via the DOSKUTSU_LOG_TAG env var so a
+// multi-config bisect can write each run's SDL trace to a unique
+// filename without renames. When unset (empty/null), the default
+// basename "sdldbg.log" is used; when set to e.g. "R1", the basename
+// is "R1SDL.LOG". The tag is capped at 5 chars when composing the
+// "<TAG>SDL.LOG" basename so "<TAG>SDL" stays deterministically inside
+// DOS 8.3 -- previously an over-long tag was silently truncated by the
+// filesystem, which could collide the SDL log onto the engine's
+// "<TAG>.LOG" basename (SESSION-SNAPSHOT-2026-05-15 finding #5). The
+// "SDL" infix keeps the SDL and engine logs distinct inside LOGS/.
 static const char *doskutsu_dbg_resolve_path(void)
 {
-    if (g_dbg_log_path[0] == '\0') {
-        const char *tag = SDL_getenv("DOSKUTSU_LOG_TAG");
-        if (tag && tag[0] != '\0') {
-            SDL_snprintf(g_dbg_log_path, sizeof(g_dbg_log_path),
-                         "/DOSKUTSU/%sSDL.LOG", tag);
-        } else {
-            SDL_strlcpy(g_dbg_log_path, "/DOSKUTSU/sdldbg.log",
-                        sizeof(g_dbg_log_path));
-        }
+    if (g_dbg_log_path[0] != '\0') {
+        return g_dbg_log_path;
+    }
+
+    // Compose the per-run basename: "<TAG>SDL.LOG" when DOSKUTSU_LOG_TAG
+    // is set (tag capped at 5 chars so "<TAG>SDL" fits DOS 8.3), else
+    // the default "sdldbg.log".
+    char log_basename[16];
+    const char *tag = SDL_getenv("DOSKUTSU_LOG_TAG");
+    if (tag && tag[0] != '\0') {
+        char shorttag[6]; // 5 tag chars + NUL; SDL_strlcpy truncates to fit
+        SDL_strlcpy(shorttag, tag, sizeof(shorttag));
+        SDL_snprintf(log_basename, sizeof(log_basename), "%sSDL.LOG", shorttag);
+    } else {
+        SDL_strlcpy(log_basename, "sdldbg.log", sizeof(log_basename));
     }
+
+    // Place the log in the "LOGS" subdir. mkdir() defensively; an EEXIST
+    // failure is success for our purposes. Any other failure (read-only
+    // volume, etc.) -> fall back to the un-prefixed dir so the trace is
+    // never lost. DJGPP/DOS accept '/' as the path separator.
+    int logs_dir_ok = 0;
+    if (mkdir("/DOSKUTSU/LOGS", 0777) == 0 || errno == EEXIST) {
+        logs_dir_ok = 1;
+    }
+
+    SDL_snprintf(g_dbg_log_path, sizeof(g_dbg_log_path), "%s/%s",
+                 logs_dir_ok ? "/DOSKUTSU/LOGS" : "/DOSKUTSU",
+                 log_basename);
     return g_dbg_log_path;
 }
 
